  number  = {11},
  pages   = {1651--1667},
  note    = {The source of the decomposition the colour-algebra section depends on: fixing one imaginary unit reduces $\mathrm{Aut}(\mathbb{O}) = G_2$ to the stabilizer $\mathrm{SU}(3)$, under which $\mathrm{Im}(\mathbb{O})$ splits as $\mathbb{R}\oplus\mathbb{C}^3$ with the quark triplet and antitriplet as complex-conjugate (NOT self-dual) summands. That non-self-duality is the input the $\mathrm{Sym}^2$ gate consumes: a self-dual 3 would carry a singlet in $\mathrm{Sym}^2$ and fail. Added 2026-08-25 — the corpus named 'the G{\"u}naydin–G{\"u}rsey decomposition' in 7+ places (color-su3-from-g2.md, schur-weyl-eightfold.md, sm-colour-stabilizer-action.md, OctonionSU3Stabilizer.lean, OctonionSU3BracketClosure.lean, ColourComplexStructure.lean) with NO bibliography entry, and OctonionSU3Stabilizer.lean backed it with '-- Ref: [manuscript]' pointing at the corpus's own audit doc. NO DOI RECORDED: api.crossref.org is blocked by the sandbox proxy (403), so the DOI could not be verified from a primary source and is deliberately omitted rather than written from memory. The volume/issue/page above are corroborated by three independent in-repo bibliographies that cite this work: library/arxiv-2306.13098v2 ref [7], library/arxiv-2202.06733v1 ref [69], and library/arxiv-1205.4619v1 ref [7]. Accessible modern restatement: library/arxiv-2403.00360v2 §2.3.},
}

